-- the two halves joined: over the forms identified by an observation window, every property of the
-- carrier agrees. So a quantity that differs between two forms which interconvert faster than the
-- observation cannot be stated of the substance under that observation at all — not as a convention
-- about which form to pick, but because there is no such function. For thalidomide over a day's
-- exposure this is the whole of why the single-enantiomer story cannot be told.
ic-respects : (A : Type 0) → (r : Interconv A) → (w : Nat) → (B : Type 0) → (g : Taut A (ic-within A r w) → B) → (a : A) → (b : A) → (p : isTrue (ic-within A r w a b)) → g (taut-pt a) ≡ g (taut-pt b)
ic-respects A r w B g a b p = taut-respects A (ic-within A r w) B g a b p
